assistant: I've implemented all five fixes. Here's a summary of what changed and why, mapped to the conventions `llama-server`/llama.cpp set for these figures.

## What I changed

### 1. The `tok/s` is now an accurate, comparable generation speed (the core bug)

**Before:** one number, `total_tokens / elapsed`, where `total` = Σ per-turn `(prompt + completion)` and `elapsed` = wall time since prompt start. Because an agent loop re-sends the whole conversation every turn, the prompt tokens dominate and grow quadratically, so it read ~2000 t/s while the model decoded at 30. That's not a speed — it's "cumulative prompt re-reads per second," and it climbs the longer the session runs.

**After:** two separate, honest figures in `agent_runner/src/session.rs`:
- **`generation_tokens_per_sec`** — output tokens ÷ wall time *spent generating* (prompt processing, tool execution, and think time excluded). While a turn streams it's `streamed_chars/4 ÷ attempt-generation-time`; after the turn it's the provider's output over the accumulated generation time (now threaded out of `drive_turn` as a second return value and accumulated across attempts). This is exactly what `llama-server` reports, so your Qwen/Tiel numbers will now land in the 20–40 range you expect.
- **`average_tokens_per_sec`** — the old cumulative figure, kept and clearly labeled `avg`, so the "throughput of the whole session" reading is still available and meaningful.

### 2. Averages alongside the per-second value
`avg` is shown next to the live speed, and it's the stable, cumulative figure — the per-second value stays live.

### 3. Stable, fixed-column layout
`stats_line()` now right-pads every field to a fixed width (speed/avg/speed-label and the tok field), so magnitudes changing no longer shift columns. The speed field is also the same width for the streamed-estimate (`~`) and provider cases so the label doesn't jump on the transition. The bar now looks like:

`⚡  38 t/s  ·  avg   1.02k t/s  ·  ctx ▇▇▇▇▇▇▇░ +87% 14.2k/16.4k  ·  123.4k tok  ·  3:46`

### 4. Compaction only shown when in use
The `compaction ▁…P%` field (and its ETA) is rendered only when `compaction_progress > 0` — i.e. only once the live context is past the warm-up threshold. The idle placeholder no longer names a field a live row would hide.

### 5. Human-readable units
New `format_number()` renders `874`, `12.3k`, `1.05M`, `1.5G`, trimming trailing zeros — used for total tokens and the context `cur/limit`.

